    notes: ["For two alleles with frequencies p and q, p + q = 1 and the genotype frequencies are p^2 (AA), 2pq (Aa) and q^2 (aa), summing to 1. In equilibrium these frequencies stay constant from generation to generation.", "Equilibrium needs no mutation, no migration, no natural selection, a very large population and random mating. The frequency of the recessive phenotype equals q^2, so q is its square root."],
